hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1730","**\nNarrated to us Abu Ja‘far Muhammad ibn Abul-Husayn as-Simmani — narrated to us Abu Tawbah ar-Rabi‘ ibn Nafi‘ — narrated to me al-Haytham ibn Humayd.\nAnd also narrated to me Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Aban — narrated to us ‘Abdullah ibn Yusuf — narrated to us al-Haytham — narrated to me Abu Ma‘bad, who is Hafs ibn Ghaylan, from Tawus, from Abu Musa al-Ash‘ari (RA), who said:\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Verily, Allah will raise up the days on the Day of Resurrection in their original form. And He will raise up the Day of Friday shining and radiant, its people surrounding it like a bride being led to her noble husband. It will illuminate for them, and they will walk in its light. Their complexions will be white like snow, and their fragrance will waft like musk. They will tread through mountains of camphor. The two weighty groups (mankind and jinn) will gaze at them in awe, unable to utter a word until they enter Paradise. None will accompany them except the mu’adhdhins who perform ihtisab (voluntary callers to prayer who also exhort good and forbid evil).”\n\nThis is the narration of Zakariyya ibn Yahya."
